@model string
@*
    The single place stored content HTML is emitted unencoded.

    Html.Raw is safe here and nowhere else, for one specific reason: this value was produced by
    RichTextRenderer, which HTML-encodes its input before adding any markup, so the string cannot
    contain a tag the renderer did not construct. Nothing user-supplied and nothing fetched from
    outside ever reaches this partial.

    Keeping it in one file rather than calling Html.Raw at each site means there is exactly one
    place to audit, and a grep for Html.Raw across the project has exactly one hit to explain.
*@
<div class="prose">@Html.Raw(Model)</div>
